day_06_forest
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/hotel_placeholder.jpg" fade="0.0"]
Narrator: Arlette is behind the reception desk when Catherine comes downstairs.
join Arlette center
Arlette: Are you leaving today? Catherine?
catherine: I suppose my stay has come to an end.
Arlette: I shall miss having someone interesting to gossip about.
catherine: I thought you were supposed to be courteous.
Arlette: I am courteous. I never said I was innocent.
- Leave Arlette with hope
	catherine: Thank you for giving me somewhere to stay.
	Arlette: You are welcome.
	catherine: If you ever hear another strange story about this town, remember that sometimes the creature in the story has a reason for what it does.
	Arlette: You sound almost fond of them.
	catherine: Perhaps I am, I came here hoping for something and I didn’t get it. But I think I got something different.
	Arlette:  Cheer yourself up, Catherine. This isn't over until it is.
	catherine: What does that even mean?
	Arlette: I don’t know. Well, all I can say is I was enchanted to meet you.
	catherine: Same, friends?
	Arlette: Friends
	set {ChapterTracking.current_day} = 0
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} += 1.0
- Warn Arlette about Marloch
	catherine:  If anyone asks about me after I leave, tell them not to follow my path.
	Arlette: Why?
	catherine: Because some wishes are better left unanswered.
	Arlette: What happened?
	catherine: I found what I came looking for. I wish I hadn't.
	Arlette: And?
	catherine: I know you are searching for something yourself. But don’t get too deep in this, sometimes, fate is fate. Trying to change it will lead to worst outcomes.
	Arlette: That is a lesson I had learn a long time ago. That’s the whole reason I have to stay here.
	set {ChapterTracking.is_evil} = true
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} -= 1.0
jump day_06_monster/